printf and its kin read every integer as a long, which only holds where an int
is passed in a slot that has been sign extended, as mescc does. With tcc on
x86_64 an int arrives in a register whose upper half is not, so -1 printed as
4294967295. Narrow it to an int, or an unsigned, unless the l modifier is there.

